WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.960
We've spent the last two and a half days going
through all the submissions and various other

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.020
reports from the Council in relation to the
Long Term Plan, which looks forwards 10 years.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.420
I think the main things are pretty clearly,
the new stadium that we've ticked off for

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.900
Coldstream Road, Northern Rangiora.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.159
It's a very big project in the history of
this district, but I think quite clearly by

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:36.320
the submissions, it severely needed and very
much wanted by a large part of our community

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:42.260
and while we recognise it's expensive, it
will add a huge amount to our sporting and

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.580
recreational provision in the district.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.520
For me personally, I think probably the most
important thing is our continuation of the

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:56.940
programme in the Redzones, now called Regeneration
Areas of Kaiapoi and also Pines/Kairaki.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:02.780
It's proceding of course, new roads are going
in as we speak, but all on top of that, as

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:05.800
we develop sportfields and other recreational
things in Kaiapoi.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.120
It will be really good to see that happening
over the next year and following years.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:17.000
And of course we also dealt with the question
of refuse collection, the famous three bins

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.640
discussion that's been going on for years
and we seem to have consulted to death.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.620
We had to do it again this year, because there
are rating implications

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.880
and it gives people a choice.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.640
They can stay exactly as they are if they
wish, or very close to what they are.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.741
You can't avoid the yellow top bin, but all
the others, there's choices around it and

00:01:33.741 --> 00:01:39.180
over the next 12 months you can expect to be asked what you want to have for your particular household.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.580
It's against the background of some challenge.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:49.040
The collapse of the mixed-paper market in
China for recyclable paper is severely impacting

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:55.130
the whole country and we're not isolated in
that, so that's adding a little bit to the

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:59.400
rates for refuse collection, and that's mostly
about recyclables.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.710
So, it's been a rewarding exercise and we
want to thank everybody who submitted.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:09.569
It was very helpful to us and because we had
a large number of submissions, that makes

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:14.640
the job easier in many ways, because we have a very clear indication of what the community wants.

